# Keep AGENTS.md in sync

After finishing a change (before claiming done / before commit when the user asked to commit), update contributor guidance when the change is **major** or **contributor-visible**.

## Files to update (same change)

| Change touches | Update |
| --- | --- |
| Product domains, safety, tray/updater, CI invariants, branding | root [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) |
| Vue pages, stores, services, shell UI, locales patterns | [`src/AGENTS.md`](../../src/AGENTS.md) |
| Core/platform/commands, Win32, persistence paths, plugins | [`src-tauri/AGENTS.md`](../../src-tauri/AGENTS.md) |

Child files add subtree rules only; they do not replace root `AGENTS.md`.

## What counts as “must write”

Update when any of these land:

- New product domain, page, store, Core module, or platform capability
- New Tauri command / event / plugin / capability permission
- Changed safety, elevation, honesty, or cancel/progress rules
- New persistence path or settings file under app local data
- Tray, titlebar, updater, or hide-to-tray behavior change
- Validation / CI requirements contributors must run
- Renamed domains or retired “do not create” patterns

## What does **not** need an AGENTS rewrite

- Typo-only or pure formatting
- Locales string-only with no new workflow
- One-off bugfix that does not change documented invariants
- Private notes, secrets, or machine-specific paths

## How to write

- Keep entries **concise** (bullets, not essays). Prefer durable rules over changelog prose.
- Put detail next to the code it governs (child `AGENTS.md` for subtree; root for cross-cutting).
- If a feature is temporary or experimental, say so explicitly or omit until it stabilizes.
- Do not invent new domains like `common` / `manager` in docs that the architecture forbids in code.

## Done check

Before finishing major work, confirm the matching `AGENTS.md` file(s) mention the new invariant or list the new domain/command/store if contributors would otherwise miss it.
